n as administrator.  An elevated token is also used when an application is configured to always require administrative privilege or to always require maximum privilege, and the user is a member of the Administrators group.\\r\\n\\r\\nType 3 is a limited token with administrative privileges removed and administrative groups disabled.  The limited token is used when User Ac"]
